# Security requirements

- NEVER hardcode secrets, API keys, tokens, or credentials. Use env vars and
  add placeholder entries to `.env.example`.
- Validate and sanitize ALL external input (request bodies, query params,
  file uploads, webhook payloads) at the boundary.
- Database access: parameterized queries / ORM only. String-built SQL is an
  automatic task failure.
- AuthN/AuthZ: every new endpoint or route must state its auth requirement
  explicitly. "Public" must be a deliberate, commented decision.
- Dependencies: before adding one, check maintenance status and known CVEs.
  Prefer stdlib or existing deps.
- Log nothing sensitive: no passwords, tokens, full card numbers, or PII
  beyond what the feature strictly requires.
- Errors returned to clients are generic; details go to server logs only.
- If you discover an existing vulnerability while working, do not silently
  fix or ignore it — report it in the PR under "Security findings".
